{
  "tema": 9621,
  "slug": "agitese-antes-de-usarse",
  "titulo": "The passive pronominal imperative in instructions (Agítese antes de usarse)",
  "subtitulo": "Agítese antes de usarse. Sírvase frío.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Formal instructions on labels, recipes and notices use the present subjunctive + se attached: Agítese, Ábrase con cuidado, Sírvase frío, Consérvese en refrigeración. Plural when the thing is plural: Lávense las verduras.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "present subjunctive (usted form)",
            "+ se"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "A **formal, impersonal** instruction: it's a passive with **se**, written like a command."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "You'll see it on **labels**, **medicine**, **recipes**, **signs**: **Consérvese en refrigeración**, **Manténgase fuera del alcance de los niños**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "It agrees with the thing: singular **ábrase**, plural **lávense las verduras**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Adding **se** makes the word esdrújula (stress on the third-to-last syllable), so it needs a written accent: **agítese**, **sírvase**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: the label is talking to nobody and to everybody."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
